course: dictionary
lesson: 9861
title: Sync and in sync
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word sync can be a verb or a noun. To sync means to make two things happen at exactly the same time, or to make devices share the same up-to-date information. Your tablet might sync photos with your computer, so both show the same pictures.
explain: Two phrases are useful. In sync means happening together, at the same time or speed. Out of sync means not matching. A dancer who moves a beat late is out of sync with the music. Context helps: if the words around sync are about time, speed or matching, it probably means happening together.
explain: Sync can also describe people. Informally, if people are in sync, they agree or get on well and think alike. Now read this: «Lip-syncing means moving your lips to a recording instead of singing live; there have been reported cases of famous singers lip-syncing at big events, and people argue whether it is cheating or a sensible way to protect a big show from going wrong.» Lip-syncing is built from sync, so it is about matching your lips to a sound that is already recorded.
fact: Sync means to make things happen at exactly the same time, or to make devices share the same up-to-date information.
fact: «In sync» means happening together, at the same time or speed.
fact: «Out of sync» means not matching.
fact: «Lip-syncing» means moving your lips to a recording instead of singing live.
fact: Informally, people who are in sync agree or get on well and think alike.
exercise: Your phone can sync photos with your computer. What does sync mean here? | Make a photo go dark and blurry | Delete all the photos from both | Take a new picture every minute | *Make devices share the same up-to-date information
exercise: The dancers were out of sync with the music. What does out of sync mean? | Singing in a loud voice | Sitting still on the stage | *Not matching, a beat behind or ahead | Dancing very fast and very happy
exercise: «Lip-syncing means moving your lips to a recording instead of singing live.» What does lip-syncing mean? | *Moving your lips to a recording instead of singing live | Reading a book out loud to a class | Whispering a secret to a friend | Singing very loudly into a microphone
test: Ava and Sam always agree and think alike, so they are... | Out of sync | Lip-syncing | Dancing late | *In sync
test: The video and the sound did not match, so the film was out of sync. What does out of sync mean? | Sung at a big event | Recorded a long time ago | Happening together at the same speed | *Not matching
exam: Mia says, «We are totally in sync, we always agree.» What does in sync mean here? | *Agreeing and getting on well | Late for school | Lost in the crowd | Singing in a loud voice
